{
  "raw": {
    "https://uhcno.edu/hr/jobs/index.php": {
      "title": "Jobs",
      "description": "University of Holy Cross | Jobs at UHC Skip to main content Skip to main navigation Skip to footer content University of Saint Mary Menu Close Menu Events Give MyUHC Quicklinks Student First Portal Canvas Library Student Life Directory Register Work at UHC Rental Spaces Bookstore View this site en español. Search the Site Search University of Holy Cross Apply Apply Now Freshman Application Transfer Application Master's & Doctoral Application Dual Enrollment Application Non-Degree Application Certification Application Readmit Application Admissions & Aid Office of Admissions Admission Requirements Request Information Schedule a Visit Tuition & Fees Financial Aid Admissions Events Office of Admissions Team Admissions Forms Academics Explore Academics Degrees & Programs Colleges Ways to Learn Calendars, Catalogs, & Schedules Academic Affairs Registrar Alumni & Friends Alumni & Friends UHC Merchandise Change of Address Request Transcript Request Give to UHC Alumni Referral Form About About UHC A Marianite Education Office of the President History Map & Parking Mission & Core Values Board of Trustees Accreditation Brand Identity Offices Jobs at UHC Home Human Resources Jobs University of Holy Cross is a Catholic, national, and comprehensive higher education\n                     institution known for the ability to balance liberal arts and sciences and nationally\n                     accredited professional programs. The University is acclaimed for its individualized service to a diverse student body,\n                     the integration of mind and heart in the Marianite tradition, and the academic preparation\n                     for competent professionals in service to the larger community. The University strives to live the mission through our core values of Excellence,\n                     Respect, Integrity, Inclusion, and Compassionate Service. Through these words, we\n                     educate the whole person in the true tradition of the Marianites of Holy Cross. You are a part of our team. As a member of the team of UHC, you will be expected to\n                     contribute your talents and energies to improve the environment and quality of the\n                     University, as well as the constituencies of the University. In return, you will be\n                     given opportunities to grow and advance in your career. University of Holy Cross is dedicated to: Providing students a quality education at the best price with the best service. Providing members of the team with wages and benefits comparable to others doing similar\n                        work within similar higher educational institutions and within the region. The only things we require for employment, compensation, advancement, and benefits\n                     are performance and a good team attitude; however, all employment at UHC is \"at will.\"\n                     No one will be denied opportunities or benefits on the basis of race, color, religion,\n                     sex, national origin, age, marital status, veteran's status, or disability that does\n                     not prohibit performance of essential job functions; nor will anyone receive special\n                     treatment for those reasons. To join the University of Holy Cross team, see the job opportunities posted below\n                     and provide the requested information. This will be forwarded to the head of the search\n                     committee for the particular job you are applying. If your qualifications meet our\n                     needs, someone will contact you to set up an interview with the committee. If your\n                     qualifications do not meet the needs for that particular job, we do keep your information\n                     on file for six months in the event that another position would become available more\n                     suited to your qualifications. UHC assures equal opportunity for all qualified persons without regard to race, color,\n                     religion, sex, national origin, age, handicap, marital status, or veteran's status\n                     in the admission to, participation in, or employment of its programs and activities. Current Employment Opportunities Director of Facilities & Campus Operations Adjunct Instructor – Doctorate in Executive Leadership Program Nursing Faculty - Full-Time and Part-Time Positions Adjunct Instructor - Accounting Adjunct Instructor - Physics Navigation Employment Opportunities Ready to Enroll? Request Information Schedule a Visit Apply Now Facebook Twitter LinkedIn YouTube Instagram University of Holy Cross 4123 Woodland Dr. New Orleans, LA 70131 (504) 394-7744 A-Z List Canvas Email Directory Map & Parking News Calendar Café & Dining Admissions Financial Aid Academics Library Counseling Center Employment Police Department Title IX © Copyright 2026. All Rights Reserved. By using this site, you agree to our privacy. Read our privacy policy. Accept ©"
    },
    "https://uhcno.edu/hr/jobs/director-facilities-campus-operations.php": {
      "title": "University of Holy Cross | Director of Facilities & Campus Operations",
      "description": "University of Holy Cross | Director of Facilities & Campus Operations Skip to main content Skip to main navigation Skip to footer content University of Saint Mary Menu Close Menu Events Give MyUHC Quicklinks Student First Portal Canvas Library Student Life Directory Register Work at UHC Rental Spaces Bookstore View this site en español. Search the Site Search University of Holy Cross Apply Apply Now Freshman Application Transfer Application Master's & Doctoral Application Dual Enrollment Application Non-Degree Application Certification Application Readmit Application Admissions & Aid Office of Admissions Admission Requirements Request Information Schedule a Visit Tuition & Fees Financial Aid Admissions Events Office of Admissions Team Admissions Forms Academics Explore Academics Degrees & Programs Colleges Ways to Learn Calendars, Catalogs, & Schedules Academic Affairs Registrar Alumni & Friends Alumni & Friends UHC Merchandise Change of Address Request Transcript Request Give to UHC Alumni Referral Form About About UHC A Marianite Education Office of the President History Map & Parking Mission & Core Values Board of Trustees Accreditation Brand Identity Offices Home Human Resources Jobs Director of Facilities & Campus Operations Director of Facilities & Campus Operations Title: Director of Facilities & Campus Operations Department: Administration / Operations Reports To: Dr. Stanton McNeely, President FLSA Status: Exempt Location: On-site - University of Holy Cross, 4123 Woodland Drive, New Orleans, Louisiana 70131 Role Overview The Director of Facilities & Campus Operations provides strategic and hands-on leadership\n                        for the safe, reliable, attractive, and efficient operation of the University of Holy\n                        Cross campus. The Director leads facilities personnel and external service partners\n                        while building a proactive, service-oriented facilities program that anticipates needs,\n                        protects institutional assets, and supports the University’s academic mission and\n                        Catholic values. Core Competencies Proactive stewardship-  Notices emerging needs, acts early, and uses inspections and\n                           data to prevent service failures rather than merely responding to them. People leadership - Builds trust, develops staff capability, sets clear expectations,\n                           and holds the team accountable with fairness and consistency. Operational judgment- Balances safety, urgency, cost, campus impact, and long-term\n                           asset condition when establishing priorities. Service orientation- Communicates respectfully, follows through, and treats facilities\n                           work as a direct contributor to the student and employee experience. Financial discipline - Makes resource-conscious decisions, manages contracts carefully,\n                           and distinguishes immediate repairs from strategic capital needs. Mission alignment- Demonstrates respect for the University’s Catholic identity and\n                           supports a welcoming, community-centered campus environment. Core Responsibilities Facilities Leadership Lead, coach, schedule, evaluate, and develop facilities, maintenance, grounds, custodial,\n                           and other assigned operations staff. Establish clear performance expectations, safety practices, work standards, communication\n                           routines, and accountability for staff and contractors. Foster a collaborative, service-minded team culture that treats faculty, staff, students,\n                           visitors, and vendors with professionalism and respect. Assess staffing, skill, coverage, and training needs; participate in recruitment,\n                           onboarding, performance management, and succession planning. Maintain a regular, visible presence throughout campus and model a proactive, solutions-oriented\n                           approach to facilities service. Proactive Maintenance Develop, implement, and continuously improve a preventive and predictive maintenance\n                           program for campus buildings, grounds, utility systems, equipment, and life-safety\n                           systems. Conduct routine campus and building inspections to identify deferred maintenance,\n                           safety hazards, operational risks, appearance issues, and repair needs before they\n                           become urgent. Establish work-order priorities, service-level expectations, tracking practices, and\n                           follow-up procedures that improve response time and stakeholder communication. Maintain accurate records for maintenance history, warranties, inspections, equipment\n                           inventories, asset condition, and planned replacements. Use a computerized maintenance management system or similar tools to track work, analyze\n                           trends, plan labor and materials, and report on outcomes. Operations and Assets Direct the maintenance, repair, and operational oversight of campus buildings, building\n                           systems, grounds, walkways, parking areas, furnishings, and related equipment. Oversee HVAC, electrical, plumbing, roofing, building envelope, fire/life-safety,\n                           access, and other critical systems through internal staff and qualified contractors. Coordinate seasonal, weather-related, and special-event preparation, including readiness\n                           for classes, campus gatherings, public events, and holidays. Partner with campus leaders to support space utilization, furniture needs, office\n                           and classroom moves, minor renovations, and operational logistics. Maintain attractive, safe, accessible, and welcoming campus conditions that reflect\n                           institutional standards and community pride. Budget, Vendors, and Projects Prepare and manage the annual facilities operating budget, including labor, supplies,\n                           utilities, maintenance contracts, equipment, and contingency needs. Develop multi-year forecasts for deferred maintenance, equipment replacement, capital\n                           renewal, and campus improvement priorities. Source, evaluate, negotiate, and manage vendors and service contracts; ensure work\n                           is competitively procured when appropriate, properly documented, completed to standard,\n                           and within budget. Develop scopes of work, specifications, bid materials, and cost estimates in collaboration\n                           with Finance, Procurement, and external technical resources. Lead or coordinate small to mid-sized renovation, repair, renewal, and capital projects\n                           from planning through closeout. Monitor contractor performance, site safety, workmanship, schedule, insurance, warranties,\n                           and final documentation. Safety, Compliance, and Resilience Maintain compliance with applicable building, fire, environmental, occupational safety,\n                           accessibility, and public-health requirements. Oversee routine testing, inspection, recordkeeping, and corrective action for applicable\n                           life-safety systems and facilities-related compliance obligations. Partner with University leadership, security, risk management, and emergency-response\n                           stakeholders to maintain and improve emergency preparedness, business continuity,\n                           and incident-response plans. Establish facilities readiness plans for hurricanes, severe weather, flooding, utility\n                           disruptions, and other events relevant to the New Orleans area. Promote safe work practices, including appropriate training, personal protective equipment,\n                           contractor safety expectations, and incident reporting. Identify energy-conservation, water-efficiency, waste-reduction, and sustainability\n                           opportunities that reduce operating cost and strengthen campus stewardship. Comparable facilities roles assign accountability for life-safety systems, regulatory\n                           compliance, emergency planning, environmental practices, energy management, and continuity\n                           planning. Campus Partnership Serve as the primary facilities liaison to academic departments, student-facing offices,\n                           events, administrative departments, and senior leadership. Communicate facilities priorities, planned disruptions, project status, emergency\n                           updates, and service expectations clearly and promptly. Translate technical issues into practical recommendations that enable leadership to\n                           make informed operational and financial decisions. Develop key performance indicators and regular reports covering work-order performance,\n                           preventive-maintenance completion, asset condition, budget performance, project status,\n                           and customer service. Perform other related duties consistent with the needs of a small, mission-driven\n                           university. Ideal Candidate Attributes Bachelor’s degree in facilities management, construction management, engineering,\n                           business, operations, or a related field; relevant combination of education, technical\n                           training, and progressively responsible experience may be considered. Five to eight years of progressively responsible facilities, building operations,\n                           maintenance, construction, or campus operations experience. At least three years of direct people-management experience, including supervision\n                           of maintenance, custodial, grounds, operations, or skilled-trades personnel. Demonstrated experience managing preventive maintenance, work orders, vendors, contracts,\n                           budgets, and operational projects. Working knowledge of building systems, including HVAC, plumbing, electrical, fire/life-safety,\n                           building envelope, and grounds operations. Demonstrated ability to inspect facilities, identify risks and deficiencies, prioritize\n                           work, and make sound operational decisions. Strong written, verbal, interpersonal, organizational, and customer-service skills. Ability to respond to after-hours emergencies and support weather or other campus\n                           emergency operations as needed. Experience in education, healthcare, hospitality, or another multi-building, customer-facing\n                           environment. Familiarity with CMMS, building automation systems, energy management systems, and\n                           Microsoft Office or comparable business tools. Experience with Louisiana building, fire, safety, accessibility, and environmental\n                           requirements. Relevant professional credential, such as Certified Facility Manager, Facilities Management\n                           Professional, Project Management Professional, or trade licensure/certification. Applicants who meet the qualifications listed above are invited to submit a complete\n                        application packet, consisting of a cover letter and resume to Shavondra Wallace at hr@uhcno.edu in a single submission. Incomplete application packets will not be considered. Equal Opportunity The University of Holy Cross assures equal opportunity for all qualified persons without\n                        regard to race, color, religion, sex, national origin, age, handicap, marital status,\n                        or veterans’ status in the admission to, participation in, or employment of its programs\n                        and activities. Navigation Employment Opportunities Ready to Enroll? Request Information Schedule a Visit Apply Now Facebook Twitter LinkedIn YouTube Instagram University of Holy Cross 4123 Woodland Dr. New Orleans, LA 70131 (504) 394-7744 A-Z List Canvas Email Directory Map & Parking News Calendar Café & Dining Admissions Financial Aid Academics Library Counseling Center Employment Police Department Title IX © Copyright 2026. All Rights Reserved. By using this site, you agree to our privacy. Read our privacy policy. Accept ©"
    },
    "https://uhcno.edu/hr/jobs/adjunct-instructor-dielp.php": {
      "title": "University of Holy Cross | Adjunct Instructor – Doctorate in Executive Leadership Program",
      "description": "University of Holy Cross | Adjunct Instructor – Doctorate in Executive Leadership Program Skip to main content Skip to main navigation Skip to footer content University of Saint Mary Menu Close Menu Events Give MyUHC Quicklinks Student First Portal Canvas Library Student Life Directory Register Work at UHC Rental Spaces Bookstore View this site en español. Search the Site Search University of Holy Cross Apply Apply Now Freshman Application Transfer Application Master's & Doctoral Application Dual Enrollment Application Non-Degree Application Certification Application Readmit Application Admissions & Aid Office of Admissions Admission Requirements Request Information Schedule a Visit Tuition & Fees Financial Aid Admissions Events Office of Admissions Team Admissions Forms Academics Explore Academics Degrees & Programs Colleges Ways to Learn Calendars, Catalogs, & Schedules Academic Affairs Registrar Alumni & Friends Alumni & Friends UHC Merchandise Change of Address Request Transcript Request Give to UHC Alumni Referral Form About About UHC A Marianite Education Office of the President History Map & Parking Mission & Core Values Board of Trustees Accreditation Brand Identity Offices Home Human Resources Jobs Adjunct Instructor – Doctorate in Executive Leadership Program Adjunct Instructor – Doctorate in Executive Leadership Program The Department of Education invites applications for an Adjunct Instructor to teach EXL 805: Change and Entrepreneurship, for Fall Semester, 2026, ONLY. Qualifications: Earned terminal degree At Least three -years (3) of experience post terminal degree attainment Experience in the workforce to include leadership positions such as CEO, department\n                        heads, or administrators. Experience with teaching using zoom platform Applicants who meet the qualifications listed above are invited to submit a complete\n                     application packet, consisting of a cover letter, resume, transcripts, and three letters\n                     of recommendation to Dr. Donaldo Batiste ( dbatiste@uchno.edu ) a single submission. Incomplete application packets will not be considered. Deadline to apply is August 3, 2026 . Equal Opportunity The University of Holy Cross assures equal opportunity for all qualified persons without\n                     regard to race, color, religion, sex, national origin, age, handicap, marital status,\n                     or veterans’ status in the admission to, participation in, or employment of its programs\n                     and activities. Navigation Employment Opportunities Ready to Enroll? Request Information Schedule a Visit Apply Now Facebook Twitter LinkedIn YouTube Instagram University of Holy Cross 4123 Woodland Dr. New Orleans, LA 70131 (504) 394-7744 A-Z List Canvas Email Directory Map & Parking News Calendar Café & Dining Admissions Financial Aid Academics Library Counseling Center Employment Police Department Title IX © Copyright 2026. All Rights Reserved. By using this site, you agree to our privacy. Read our privacy policy. Accept ©"
    },
    "https://uhcno.edu/hr/jobs/nursing-faculty.php": {
      "title": "University of Holy Cross",
      "description": "University of Holy Cross | Nursing Faculty – Full-Time and Part-Time Positions Skip to main content Skip to main navigation Skip to footer content University of Saint Mary Menu Close Menu Events Give MyUHC Quicklinks Student First Portal Canvas Library Student Life Directory Register Work at UHC Rental Spaces Bookstore View this site en español. Search the Site Search University of Holy Cross Apply Apply Now Freshman Application Transfer Application Master's & Doctoral Application Dual Enrollment Application Non-Degree Application Certification Application Readmit Application Admissions & Aid Office of Admissions Admission Requirements Request Information Schedule a Visit Tuition & Fees Financial Aid Admissions Events Office of Admissions Team Admissions Forms Academics Explore Academics Degrees & Programs Colleges Ways to Learn Calendars, Catalogs, & Schedules Academic Affairs Registrar Alumni & Friends Alumni & Friends UHC Merchandise Change of Address Request Transcript Request Give to UHC Alumni Referral Form About About UHC A Marianite Education Office of the President History Map & Parking Mission & Core Values Board of Trustees Accreditation Brand Identity Offices Home Human Resources Jobs Nursing Faculty – Full-Time and Part-Time Positions Nursing Faculty - Full-Time and Part-Time Positions The Department of Nursing at the University of Holy Cross invites applications for\n                     faculty positions in the Bachelor of Science in Nursing Program. These positions are\n                     pivotal in ensuring the delivery of high-quality nursing education, fostering academic\n                     excellence and innovative teaching that meets the needs for nurses in the community,\n                     and committing to our mission of educating the minds and hearts of our students. Required Education and Experience Current unencumbered license to practice as a registered nurse in the State of Louisiana. Master's degree in Nursing as well as a Bachelor of Science in Nursing degree. * At least three (3) years of clinical experience in the area of teaching responsibility. *An exception to the Master’s degree in nursing may be made if the registered nurse\n                        holds a baccalaureate degree in nursing and has three years of nursing practice in\n                        a clinical setting.  The Chair will submit a request for approval of faculty exception\n                        to Louisiana State Board of Nursing.  If LSBN approves the faculty exception, the\n                        potential faculty must be enrolled in a Master’s in nursing program and have a written\n                        plan on file designating a plan to complete the Master’s in nursing program within\n                        two (2) calendar years. Applicants who meet the qualifications listed above are invited to submit a complete\n                        application packet, consisting of a cover letter, resume, official transcripts, and\n                        three letters of recommendation to Shawna Mitchell-Johnson at smitchell@uhcno.edu in a single submission . Incomplete application packets will not be considered. Equal Opportunity The University of Holy Cross assures equal opportunity for all qualified persons without\n                        regard to race, color, religion, sex, national origin, age, handicap, marital status,\n                        or veterans’ status in the admission to, participation in, or employment of its programs\n                        and activities. Navigation Employment Opportunities Ready to Enroll? Request Information Schedule a Visit Apply Now Facebook Twitter LinkedIn YouTube Instagram University of Holy Cross 4123 Woodland Dr. New Orleans, LA 70131 (504) 394-7744 A-Z List Canvas Email Directory Map & Parking News Calendar Café & Dining Admissions Financial Aid Academics Library Counseling Center Employment Police Department Title IX © Copyright 2026. All Rights Reserved. By using this site, you agree to our privacy. Read our privacy policy. Accept ©"
    },
    "https://uhcno.edu/hr/jobs/adjunct-instructor-accounting.php": {
      "title": "University of Holy Cross | Adjunct Instructor - Accounting",
      "description": "University of Holy Cross | Adjunct Instructor - Accounting Skip to main content Skip to main navigation Skip to footer content University of Saint Mary Menu Close Menu Events Give MyUHC Quicklinks Student First Portal Canvas Library Student Life Directory Register Work at UHC Rental Spaces Bookstore View this site en español. Search the Site Search University of Holy Cross Apply Apply Now Freshman Application Transfer Application Master's & Doctoral Application Dual Enrollment Application Non-Degree Application Certification Application Readmit Application Admissions & Aid Office of Admissions Admission Requirements Request Information Schedule a Visit Tuition & Fees Financial Aid Admissions Events Office of Admissions Team Admissions Forms Academics Explore Academics Degrees & Programs Colleges Ways to Learn Calendars, Catalogs, & Schedules Academic Affairs Registrar Alumni & Friends Alumni & Friends UHC Merchandise Change of Address Request Transcript Request Give to UHC Alumni Referral Form About About UHC A Marianite Education Office of the President History Map & Parking Mission & Core Values Board of Trustees Accreditation Brand Identity Offices Home Human Resources Jobs Adjunct Instructor - Accounting Adjunct Instructor - Accounting The Department of Business Administration invites applications for a part-time Accounting Instructor to teach Individual and Business Taxation courses for accounting majors. Qualifications: Required industry experience in taxation Master’s degree in Accounting or a Master’s degree in a related field with at least\n                        18 graduate credit hours in Accounting Knowledge of Canvas Learning Management System. Experience with teaching using zoom platform This position offers an opportunity to teach motivated accounting students and contribute\n                     to the academic mission of the Department of Business Administration. Applicants who meet the qualifications listed above are invited to submit a complete\n                        application packet, consisting of a cover letter, resume, transcripts, and three letters\n                        of recommendation to Jennifer Jeansonne, jennifer.jeansonne@uhcno.edu in a single submission. Incomplete application packets will not be considered. Equal Opportunity The University of Holy Cross assures equal opportunity for all qualified persons without\n                        regard to race, color, religion, sex, national origin, age, handicap, marital status,\n                        or veterans’ status in the admission to, participation in, or employment of its programs\n                        and activities. Navigation Employment Opportunities Ready to Enroll? Request Information Schedule a Visit Apply Now Facebook Twitter LinkedIn YouTube Instagram University of Holy Cross 4123 Woodland Dr. New Orleans, LA 70131 (504) 394-7744 A-Z List Canvas Email Directory Map & Parking News Calendar Café & Dining Admissions Financial Aid Academics Library Counseling Center Employment Police Department Title IX © Copyright 2026. All Rights Reserved. By using this site, you agree to our privacy. Read our privacy policy. Accept ©"
    },
    "https://uhcno.edu/hr/jobs/adjunct-instructor-physics.php": {
      "title": "University of Holy Cross | Adjunct Instructor - Physics",
      "description": "University of Holy Cross | Adjunct Instructor - Physics Skip to main content Skip to main navigation Skip to footer content University of Saint Mary Menu Close Menu Events Give MyUHC Quicklinks Student First Portal Canvas Library Student Life Directory Register Work at UHC Rental Spaces Bookstore View this site en español. Search the Site Search University of Holy Cross Apply Apply Now Freshman Application Transfer Application Master's & Doctoral Application Dual Enrollment Application Non-Degree Application Certification Application Readmit Application Admissions & Aid Office of Admissions Admission Requirements Request Information Schedule a Visit Tuition & Fees Financial Aid Admissions Events Office of Admissions Team Admissions Forms Academics Explore Academics Degrees & Programs Colleges Ways to Learn Calendars, Catalogs, & Schedules Academic Affairs Registrar Alumni & Friends Alumni & Friends UHC Merchandise Change of Address Request Transcript Request Give to UHC Alumni Referral Form About About UHC A Marianite Education Office of the President History Map & Parking Mission & Core Values Board of Trustees Accreditation Brand Identity Offices Home Human Resources Jobs Adjunct Instructor - Physics Adjunct Instructor - Physics The University of Holy Cross invites applications for the position of Adjunct Instructor\n                     of Physics. The position starts August 12, 2025, for late afternoon in-person classes.\n                     Review of applications is ongoing. Position Description Adjunct Instructor of Physics is a part-time faculty position. The instructor is contracted\n                     per course on a semester-by-semester basis. Responsibilities Planning and delivering instruction, testing, and reporting in the assigned Physics\n                     course(s) in accordance with course description, syllabus, learning outcomes, and\n                     University policies. The instructor must also be available for student conferences\n                     to review individual student progress. Additional responsibilities include maintaining\n                     student attendance records and adhering to academic calendar deadlines. The Adjunct\n                     Instructor must demonstrate the ability to effectively educate students and to exemplify\n                     the mission of the University to educate the minds and hearts of its students. Qualifications This position requires a master’s degree or higher in Physics or in a closely related\n                     field with at least 18 documented graduate-level credit hours in Physics coursework.\n                     At least one year of experience as an instructor (full-time or adjunct) is preferred,\n                     as is experience with learning management systems. The instructor must possess exemplary\n                     interpersonal skills, ability to work effectively with a wide range of students, and\n                     skills in establishing and managing course content and academic deadlines. Equal Opportunity The University of Holy Cross assures equal opportunity for all qualified persons without\n                     regard to race, color, religion, sex, national origin, age, handicap, marital status,\n                     or veterans’ status in the admission to, participation in, or employment of its programs\n                     and activities. Applicants who meet the qualifications listed above are invited to submit a complete\n                     application packet, consisting of a cover letter, resume, transcripts, and three letters\n                     of recommendation to Jennifer Jeansonne, jennifer.jeansonne@uhcno.edu in a single submission. Incomplete application packets will not be considered. Navigation Employment Opportunities Ready to Enroll? Request Information Schedule a Visit Apply Now Facebook Twitter LinkedIn YouTube Instagram University of Holy Cross 4123 Woodland Dr. New Orleans, LA 70131 (504) 394-7744 A-Z List Canvas Email Directory Map & Parking News Calendar Café & Dining Admissions Financial Aid Academics Library Counseling Center Employment Police Department Title IX © Copyright 2026. All Rights Reserved. By using this site, you agree to our privacy. Read our privacy policy. Accept ©"
    },
